hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19201","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Ibn Khuthaym from Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Rifaah from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The freed client of a people is from them, and their sister's son is from them, and their ally is from them."
"19202","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Khuthaym from Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Rifaah from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered Quraysh and said: Is there among you any outsider? They said: No, except our sister's son, our ally, and our freedman. He said: Your sister's son is from you, your ally is from you, and your freedman is from you. Quraysh are people of truthfulness and trust, so whoever seeks evil against them Allah will throw him into the Fire on his face."
"19203","Affan narrated to us, Bishr meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us from Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Rafi ibn Rafi al-Zuraqi from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our ally is from us, our freedman is from us, and our sister's son is from us."
"19204","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad al-Zuraqi from Rifaah ibn Rafi al-Zuraqi, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque, and he prayed near him, then he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Repeat your prayer, for you did not pray. He returned and prayed like what he had prayed, then he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to him: Repeat your prayer, for you did not pray. He said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me how to act. He said: When you face the qiblah then say takbir, then recite the Mother of the Quran, then recite what you wish. When you bow then place your palms on your knees, extend your back, and settle your bowing. When you raise your head then straighten your spine until the bones return to their joints. When you prostrate then settle your prostration. When you raise your head then sit on your left thigh. Then do that in every rakah and prostration."
"19205","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik from Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir from Ali ibn Yahya al-Zuraqi from his father from Rifaah ibn Rafi al-Zuraqi who said: We were praying one day behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, a man behind him said: Our Lord, to You is praise, abundant, good, blessed praise. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished he said: Who was the speaker just now? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw more than thirty angels racing to it, which of them writes it first."
"19206","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad narrated to us from his father from his uncle, and he was a Badri, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque. A man entered and prayed in a corner of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept watching him. Then he came and greeted, he returned it to him and said: Go back and pray, for you did not pray. He said it two or three times. He said to him on the third or fourth: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have exerted myself, so teach me and show me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you intend to pray then perform wudu and perfect your wudu, then face the qiblah, then say takbir, then recite, then bow until you are tranquil while bowing, then rise until you are tranquil standing, then prostrate until you are tranquil prostrating, then rise until you are tranquil sitting, then prostrate until you are tranquil prostrating, then stand. If you complete your prayer in this manner you have completed it, and whatever you diminish of this you only diminish from your prayer."
